 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2021-02-03",
   "text": "Medical Debt Relief Act of 2021 \n This bill modifies requirements related to the reporting of medical debt. Specifically, a consumer reporting agency is prohibited from adding medical debt information to a consumer credit report if the debt \n was fully paid or settled, or \n is less than a year old. \n Additionally, a debt collector must notify the consumer prior to reporting medical debt to a consumer reporting agency."
  }
 ],
